<!doctype html>
<html class="js" lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}" dir="ltr" data-froya-nav="b" data-country="{{ localization.country.iso_code }}" data-currency="{{ localization.country.currency.iso_code }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  {%- comment -%}
    The store sells from the home page only, so product pages (reached from Google Shopping, order
    emails, the Shop app…) send the visitor straight to the home page. A theme cannot answer with a
    real 301 and Shopify's URL redirects only cover paths that no longer exist, so this is a meta
    refresh backed by a script; skipped in the theme editor so the product template stays editable.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if template.name == 'product' and settings.redirect_product_pages and request.design_mode == false -%}
    {%- assign home_url = shop.url | append: routes.root_url -%}
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ home_url }}">
    <script>window.location.replace({{ home_url | json }});</script>
  {%- endif -%}
  <meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#1f1f1f">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
  {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 32, height: 32 }}">
  {%- endif -%}

  <title>
    {{ page_title }}
    {%- if current_tags %} &ndash; tagged "{{ current_tags | join: ', ' }}"{% endif -%}
    {%- if current_page != 1 %} &ndash; Page {{ current_page }}{% endif -%}
    {%- unless page_title contains shop.name %} &ndash; {{ shop.name }}{% endunless -%}
  </title>
  {% if page_description %}<meta name="description" content="{{ page_description | escape }}">{% endif %}
  {% render 'meta-tags' %}

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cdn.shopify.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Libre+Baskerville:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=Caveat:wght@400..700&display=swap">

  {{ 'critical.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {{ 'blaze.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {{ 'theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {{ 'sections-inline.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {{ 'sections.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  {%- liquid
    comment
      Theme settings → Offer colours: one gradient shared by the hero pill, the scrolling offer
      banner and the cart's code reminder. The soft version keeps the hues at partial strength so
      dark text stays readable on it.
    endcomment
    assign offer_1 = settings.offer_color_1 | default: '#dfb142'
    assign offer_2 = settings.offer_color_2 | default: '#e98044'
    assign offer_3 = settings.offer_color_3 | default: '#af8998'
    assign offer_soft = settings.offer_soft_strength | default: 45 | divided_by: 100.0
  -%}
  <style>
    :root {
      --offer-gradient: linear-gradient(92deg, {{ offer_1 }} 10%, {{ offer_2 }} 49.5%, {{ offer_3 }} 100%);
      --offer-gradient-soft: linear-gradient(92deg, {{ offer_1 | color_modify: 'alpha', offer_soft }} 10%, {{ offer_2 | color_modify: 'alpha', offer_soft }} 49.5%, {{ offer_3 | color_modify: 'alpha', offer_soft }} 100%);
      --offer-text: {{ settings.offer_text_color | default: '#ffffff' }};
      --offer-accent: {{ offer_2 }};
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    window.Shopify = window.Shopify || {};
    window.Shopify.routes = window.Shopify.routes || {};
    window.Shopify.routes.root = '{{ routes.root_url }}';
    window.theme = { moneyFormat: {{ shop.money_format | json }} };
  </script>

  {{ content_for_header }}
</head>

<body class="no-focus-outline features--image-zoom template-{{ request.page_type | handle }}{% if template.suffix %} template-{{ request.page_type | handle }}--{{ template.suffix | handle }}{% endif %}">
  {% render 'froya-svg-defs' %}

  {% sections 'header-group' %}

  <div id="main" class="anchor" role="main">
    {%- if request.page_type == 'policy' and settings.support_email != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Store policies come from Shopify admin (Settings → Policies), where Shopify's templates insert
        the store's own email and a link can show one address but open another. So on /policies/…
        pages every mailto: link opens the support email (Theme settings → Customer support) and the
        store email in the text is replaced with it, leaving the support address as the only one a
        shopper sees. Emptying that setting shows the policies exactly as written.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign support_email = settings.support_email | strip | escape -%}
      {%- assign policy_parts = content_for_layout | split: 'mailto:' -%}
      {%- capture policy_html -%}
        {{- policy_parts.first -}}
        {%- for part in policy_parts offset: 1 -%}
          {%- comment -%} The old address runs up to the first quote, bracket, "?" or space. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign old_address = part | split: '"' | first | split: "'" | first | split: '<' | first | split: '>' | first | split: '?' | first | split: ' ' | first -%}
          mailto:{{ support_email }}{{ part | remove_first: old_address }}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {%- if shop.email != blank -%}
        {%- assign policy_html = policy_html | replace: shop.email, support_email -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {{ policy_html }}
    {%- else -%}
      {{ content_for_layout }}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {% sections 'footer-group' %}

  {%- comment -%}
    Shopify only pre-selects a visitor's country on Shopify Plus. On every other plan the storefront
    opens in the primary market's default country, so a shopper abroad sees the wrong currency until
    checkout asks for an address. assets/main.js asks Shopify which country it detects for this
    visitor (browsing_context_suggestions.json, Shopify's own GeoIP) and submits this form once so the
    buy box, cart and checkout all start in the local currency. The select lists every country the
    store sells to, so a detected country the store does not serve is simply ignored.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if settings.auto_localize and localization.available_countries.size > 1 and request.design_mode == false -%}
    <div hidden>
      {%- form 'localization', id: 'localization_form_auto', data-current-country: localization.country.iso_code -%}
        <select name="country_code" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">
          {%- for country in localization.available_countries -%}
            <option value="{{ country.iso_code }}"{% if country.iso_code == localization.country.iso_code %} selected{% endif %}>{{ country.name }}</option>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </select>
      {%- endform -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <script src="{{ 'blaze-slider.min.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
  <script src="{{ 'main.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
